<section>
  ## Call site

  <code lang=cpp id=flow>
    int main() {
      auto result = process("42", 2);

      if (result) {
        std::cout << "Result: " << *result << "\n";
      } else {
        std::cout << "Error: " << result.error() << "\n";
      }

      return 0;
    }
  </code>
</section>

<section>
  ## Summary

  `and_then` is `>>=` / `flatMap`. `transform` is `fmap`/`map`. `std::expected`
  is `Either`, `std::optional` is `Maybe`. C++23 finally has what Haskell
  has had all along -- just under different names.

  Thanks!
</section>

